s.push_str("\nPrefix records remain two FqBatch vectors per eight points, 16,000/28,160 bytes at 200/352 pairs. Caller scratch/reference capacities match across all three arms and remain stable. Payload sizes exclude other arrays, stacks and allocator state. RSS is a lifetime diagnostic including setup/primes, not an isolated proof peak, minimum RAM or a pressure test. No memory saving is established.\n\n## Independent review and limits\n\n");writeln!(s,"The independent Rust reviewer imports no campaign/parser code and checks **{} source/input pins and 327 successful workflow commands and one preserved failed freeze**, normalized protocols, actual argv/stream hashes, original-source recovery, exact field/adapter identity, all 270 raw integer latency observations and paired gates, all output/capacity signatures, CPU/RSS and separately parsed PMU/profile ownership/loss. The report uses those reconstructed results.\n",r["source_pin_checks"]).unwrap();
s.push_str("No new SDK proof, independent Gnark export, AWS/Aeglos, phone/ARM/TEE, 250/4999, swap/pressure, minimum-RAM or concurrent-proof result is added. Canonical proof ledger stays **30,708**. A component pass only selects further complete-query/full-SDK/resource qualification; it never adopts a compiler artifact or completes the goal.\n\n## Accepted CPU and Metal comparisons\n\nInherited accepted 32-worker local results and supplied historical M5 references, not measurements of this candidate. [Accepted manifest](../2026-10-30-g2-vector-sign-adoption176/artifacts/production-source-manifest.json). Latest separate full-SDK evidence is the [composed PGO comparison](../2026-11-05-bundle-proof-pgo-full176/README.md), whose control-calibration failure remains closed without adoption.\n\n| Shape | Accepted local ms | M5 CPU ms | M5 Metal ms | CPU/local | Metal/local | CPU10× target ms |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");let m=read("/home/ubuntu/src/zk-tools/zopro/docs/benchmarks/2026-10-30-g2-vector-sign-adoption176/artifacts/production-source-manifest.json");for k in["1x2","2x2","4x2","8x2","12x2","16x2","24x2","merge-24x1"]{let v=&m["m5"][k];assert_eq!(v["goal10x"],false);writeln!(s,"| {k} | {:.6} | {:.0} | {:.0} | {:.3}× | {:.3}× | {:.1} |",f(&v["accepted_ms"]),f(&v["cpu_reference_ms"]),f(&v["metal_reference_ms"]),f(&v["cpu_speedup"]),f(&v["metal_speedup"]),f(&v["required_ms_for_CPU10x"])).unwrap();}
